messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: C03
Scenario title: Childcare Notices and Consent Responses
Initial workflow description:
I read messages from childcare, respond when necessary, and make sure we remember any special event or item to bring.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "Through which channel or platform do childcare messages arrive — for example, a dedicated parent portal, email, a messaging app, or physical paper notices?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "How do you currently decide whether a message needs a reply versus just needs to be read and noted — is there a consistent signal like a specific subject line, a form, or a deadline mentioned?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "When you identify a special event or an item to bring, where do you record it so you and your household remember it — for instance, a phone calendar, a shared list app, or something else?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "Roughly how many childcare messages do you receive in a typical week, and of those, how many usually require you to take some action?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "Is it just you who reads and responds to these messages, or do other caregivers also need to see and act on them?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "What happens if a response deadline or a required item is missed — do you receive a follow-up from the childcare provider, or is there no safety net currently in place?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Childcare Notices and Consent Responses with explicit responsibilities, decisions and recorded completion.",
  "actors": [
    "mother",
    "partner",
    "childcare administrator",
    "childcare teacher"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "childcare messaging app",
    "notice checklist",
    "shared family calendar",
    "response archive"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "provider notice",
    "response deadline",
    "household schedule",
    "required item details"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "classified notice",
    "submitted response",
    "calendar entry",
    "preparation reminder"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Collect unread notices from the provider app",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Identify response and preparation requirements",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Check the event against the household schedule",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Ask the administrator about unclear notice details",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Confirm the family's participation decision",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Submit a response and save the receipt",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Add the event and item deadline to the calendar",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A8",
      "name": "Check that the preparation reminder is assigned",
      "actor": "mother"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Does the notice require an explicit response?",
      "branches": [
        "submit the parent's decision",
        "record the notice without a response"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Are the event details complete and compatible with the schedule?",
      "branches": [
        "confirm the plan",
        "clarify missing details or decline participation"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "ambiguous notice",
    "schedule conflict",
    "response receipt missing",
    "preparation task unassigned"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A7",
      "to": "A8",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A2",
      "rationale": "Extract proposed dates and preparation requirements for review."
    },
    {
      "target": "A7",
      "rationale": "Draft calendar entries from confirmed notices."
    },
    {
      "target": "A8",
      "rationale": "Flag unassigned preparation reminders."
    }
  ],
  "operating_context": {
    "frequency": "notices checked once each evening in this fictional household",
    "manual_effort": "Reading and recording a routine notice takes about five minutes.",
    "data_availability": "Notices and response receipts are accessible in the provider app; the family manually copies dates into its calendar.",
    "integration_and_approval_constraints": "Consent is always confirmed by a parent; summaries cannot submit consent or disclose notices to unrelated recipients."
  },
  "interpretation": "Activity dependencies describe the nominal sequence. Decision branches and exception descriptions qualify that sequence; this is not an executable BPMN model."
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}
